{
 "koral-function": 1,
 "purpose": "Culling",
 "description": "What of an indirect draw of entities is seen, in two draws (Wihlidal's two phases), on the GPU. Two IndirectDraws in eGPU, `early` and `late`, and two Draws of them: the first \u2014 commands `early`, which draws into `depth` \u2014 draws what was seen the frame before and is in sight; a depth pyramid (HiZ) is made of what it drew; the second, loading what the first drew, draws what is in sight, was not seen the frame before and is not behind it. Whether each was seen is kept for the next frame, `count` of them. instances, stride, matrixOffset and ranges are as CullInSight's: each draw's shader finds its instance through its own `visible`.",
 "tags": [
  "cull",
  "occlusion",
  "two phase",
  "hiz",
  "depth pyramid",
  "gpu driven",
  "indirect",
  "instances",
  "visibility"
 ],
